############################
# Claude Code local settings (may contain machine-local allow-lists / secrets)
############################
**/.claude/settings.local.json

############################
# Claude Code project skills (local tooling, not part of the service)
############################
**/.claude/skills/

############################
# Application secrets
############################
# The whole secret/ directory is local-only and never committed: .env, master.key, plaintext.env,
# ghcr.token, Protect-Env.ps1 (the .env encryptor), SSH keys, etc.
secret/*

# Keys and certificates — never commit private key material.
# Covers service/docs/ssh.key and anything similar dropped alongside the docs.
*.key
*.pem
*.p12
*.pfx
*.ppk
*.jks
*.keystore
id_rsa
id_ed25519

application.yml
.env
config.ini

# Internal cproxy docs stay local-only: CLAUDE.md (real droplet/VPC/admin addresses, deploy runbook),
# and everything under docs/ EXCEPT specification.md — api-guide.html, do-update.md (the deploy
# runbook), postman-collection.json, SKILL.md and chat.skill are operational, not reference.
# specification.md and CHANGELOG.md ARE tracked; both carry <placeholder> hosts, never real ones.
service/cproxy/docs/*.*
!service/cproxy/docs/specification.md
service/cproxy/CLAUDE.md

Skills/*
docs/*